    31	// Font: the name of the font file.
    32	// String: the text string the text object is composed of.
    33	// Cuts: the number of times excess material is cut off, to form the bevel.
    34	//       More cuts will give smoother results, but take longer to render.
    35	// BevelAng: the angle of the bevel.
    36	// BevelDepth: the depth of the bevelled portion of the text.
    37	// Depth: the total depth of the text object.
    38	// Offset: the offset value for the text object.  Since the front faces of each
    39	//         letter need to be in the same plane, z values are ignored.
    40	      merge {
    41	      union {
    42	      text {ttf Font, String Depth-BevelDepth, Offset*(x+y)}
